WEBVTT

00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:14.300
Who could that be?

00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:18.910
Hey...

00:00:32.190 --> 00:00:33.030
Hey, Chelin.

00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:34.990
Oh, you're here.

00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:36.160
Sorry I'm late.

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:39.330
What took you so long?

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:40.490
I was stuck in traffic.

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:42.910
That must have been a pain.

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:46.710
Come in.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:48.420
Let me introduce you guys.

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:50.130
This is Minhyung Lee.

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:52.170
We met in France.

00:00:53.630 --> 00:00:56.430
These are my high school friends that I told you about.

00:00:57.970 --> 00:01:00.430
Nice to meet you all. I'm Minhyung.

00:01:01.930 --> 00:01:04.230
These two got engaged today.

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:05.310
Aren't they a cute couple?

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:06.990
Oh, really?

00:01:06.990 --> 00:01:08.100
Congratulations.

00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:09.900
Why thank you.

00:01:11.150 --> 00:01:14.190
We need to get going, sorry.

00:02:39.950 --> 00:02:40.740
What did you think?

00:02:41.490 --> 00:02:43.620
Friends of ten years getting engaged, huh?

00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:45.450
I can't even imagine something like that.

00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:46.870
Maybe they like complacency.

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:48.910
They <i>are</i> an odd couple, now that you mention it.

00:02:49.580 --> 00:02:51.120
Did I come at a bad time though?

00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:54.130
What do you mean?

00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:58.800
Why were all your friends so surprised to see me?

00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:02.140
I didn't want to say it out loud, but it did make me uncomfortable.

00:03:02.430 --> 00:03:03.890
Oh, that's because...

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:07.060
this is the first time I've introduced a boyfriend of mine.

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:08.930
That's probably why they were all so surprised.

00:03:09.770 --> 00:03:10.440
Really?

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:11.140
Why?

00:03:11.270 --> 00:03:12.400
Am I really the first?

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:14.190
Of course!

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:19.070
I'm just pulling your leg.

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:31.120
Hey, Yujin...

00:03:33.250 --> 00:03:34.330
Are you okay?

00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:35.210
About what?

00:03:35.330 --> 00:03:38.170
That guy Chelin's supposedly going out with...

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:40.300
He really looks like Joonsang, doesn't he?

00:03:41.050 --> 00:03:42.180
He does!

00:03:42.470 --> 00:03:46.180
I thought Joonsang had come back to life when I saw him.

00:03:47.010 --> 00:03:50.020
How could they look so much alike?

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:54.980
I was so surprised that I thought I was going to faint!

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:59.030
Oh wait, he's going to fall over now.

00:03:59.150 --> 00:04:01.030
Look! It's so funny.

00:04:03.070 --> 00:04:05.240
Hey, Yujin...

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:07.780
Today must have been hard for you, Sanghyuk.

00:04:08.580 --> 00:04:09.540
Drink up.

00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:15.250
<i>I think he's the guy that I saw on the street.</i>

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:18.590
<i>I'm such an idiot, aren't I?</i>

00:04:24.970 --> 00:04:25.890
Let me do it.

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:30.010
That Minhyung person really looked like him, right?

00:04:30.430 --> 00:04:33.520
Yeah, there was definitely a resemblance.

00:04:33.850 --> 00:04:35.550
We live in a funny world, don't we?

00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:37.520
How could something like this happen?

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:40.710
Maybe we shouldn't have invited Chelin over.

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:42.530
I'm sorry, man.

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:43.820
Don't be.

00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:49.490
Plenty of people look alike in this world.

00:04:49.700 --> 00:04:50.950
I'm kind of glad, actually.

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:56.340
At least now I know that it wasn't Joonsang she saw that day,

00:04:56.340 --> 00:04:57.580
just someone who looks like him.

00:04:57.920 --> 00:04:59.360
Yeah, don't worry about it.

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:00.590
Yujin's a strong girl.

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:02.920
Sometimes I wish she wasn't.

00:05:03.460 --> 00:05:05.550
I wish she'd be a little more honest about her feelings

00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:09.600
and tell me when she's in pain or feeling sad.

00:06:19.620 --> 00:06:21.830
Are you on your way to the presentation?

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:23.170
<i>So you do remember.</i>

00:06:23.540 --> 00:06:25.820
You talked about it the entire time we were planning the engagement party;

00:06:25.960 --> 00:06:29.010
you said you've been preparing for this presentation for three months.

00:06:29.630 --> 00:06:32.600
<i>I'm okay, Sanghyuk.</i>

00:06:32.850 --> 00:06:39.020
<i>So don't get all worked up or beat yourself up over me, okay?</i>

00:06:39.310 --> 00:06:41.560
<i>You do know what I'm talking about, right?</i>

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:43.400
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:46.860
Wish me "Good luck" on my presentation.

00:06:46.980 --> 00:06:49.990
I really think I could do well if you told me "Good luck."

00:06:50.110 --> 00:06:51.530
<i>Okay, good luck.</i>

00:06:51.700 --> 00:06:54.830
<i>I'm sure that the Yujin I know will do just fine.</i>

00:06:54.950 --> 00:06:57.370
Thanks, that really helped.

00:06:58.450 --> 00:07:00.370
I love you, Yujin.

00:07:00.790 --> 00:07:02.880
<i>Me too.</i>

00:07:07.340 --> 00:07:08.390
He'll be with you momentarily.

00:07:08.390 --> 00:07:10.220
Why don't you wait inside?

00:07:10.290 --> 00:07:11.220
Okay.

00:08:09.570 --> 00:08:10.650
What's going on?

00:08:15.780 --> 00:08:18.530
I'm sure it wasn't easy adjusting to the way I work.

00:08:19.030 --> 00:08:22.250
I wouldn't have been so anal if I'd known that you were a friend of Chelin's.

00:08:23.120 --> 00:08:26.250
Polaris, and Miss Yujin Jung,

00:08:26.630 --> 00:08:28.780
it's my firm belief

00:08:28.780 --> 00:08:31.210
that I should always get the best out of my investments.

00:08:32.340 --> 00:08:33.720
I hope you can understand that.

00:08:34.720 --> 00:08:37.970
I'll just say that I agree with the overall concept.

00:08:38.300 --> 00:08:39.600
Do you think we could go over the details

00:08:39.600 --> 00:08:41.890
of your presentation before the meeting?

00:08:51.820 --> 00:08:53.160
How is it?

00:08:53.160 --> 00:08:54.740
It looks normal, doesn't it?

00:08:55.110 --> 00:08:58.280
It has two eyes, one nose, and just a single mouth.

00:08:59.990 --> 00:09:02.240
Do you always stare at peoples' faces like that?

00:09:02.620 --> 00:09:03.330
O-Oh no, I...

00:09:06.500 --> 00:09:07.750
Was I too rude?

00:09:14.470 --> 00:09:15.340
Are you all right?

00:09:18.760 --> 00:09:19.850
Please excuse me.

00:09:21.300 --> 00:09:22.390
Miss Yujin!

00:09:27.020 --> 00:09:29.270
Why is it taking her so long to land the contract?

00:09:31.690 --> 00:09:33.110
Oh man.

00:09:33.230 --> 00:09:34.440
How was it, Seungryong?

00:09:34.940 --> 00:09:36.360
It's so cold outside.

00:09:36.950 --> 00:09:38.410
Where's Yujin? Did she land the contract?

00:09:38.530 --> 00:09:39.360
No clue.

00:09:39.360 --> 00:09:41.360
She went over there to give her presentation a while ago,

00:09:41.360 --> 00:09:42.790
but I can't even reach her on the phone.

00:09:42.990 --> 00:09:45.950
It must be because of that annoying new director guy.

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:48.960
He didn't seem all that annoying to me.

00:09:49.580 --> 00:09:53.920
How do you know that, when even Yujin hasn't met him before?

00:09:54.340 --> 00:09:56.720
This is why gathering information is important.

00:09:57.920 --> 00:09:58.420
Here.

00:09:58.930 --> 00:09:59.550
What's this?

00:09:59.680 --> 00:10:00.890
His track record's incredible, right?

00:10:01.350 --> 00:10:06.390
I thought he'd be some bald guy, not a hunk like this!

00:10:06.520 --> 00:10:08.350
Look at his profile, not his face!

00:10:08.480 --> 00:10:10.980
He's been abroad his entire life, huh?

00:10:11.080 --> 00:10:12.780
New York, Paris...

00:10:12.780 --> 00:10:14.980
Talk about being born with a silver spoon in your mouth.

00:10:15.360 --> 00:10:17.570
He's got skills, looks...

00:10:17.570 --> 00:10:19.400
could he be any more complete?

00:10:20.030 --> 00:10:23.370
What'd make him perfect is if he had a killer voice to go with all this.

00:10:24.950 --> 00:10:25.990
Yes, you've reached Polaris.

00:10:26.540 --> 00:10:28.210
This is Minhyung Lee from MARCIAN.

00:10:29.210 --> 00:10:30.580
He's perfect.

00:10:37.050 --> 00:10:37.970
Hey, Yujin.

00:10:38.720 --> 00:10:40.130
This is your first time here, right?

00:10:42.590 --> 00:10:44.370
Come, sit down.

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:46.100
Sanghyuk's doing well, I imagine?

00:10:47.390 --> 00:10:48.230
Yeah.

00:10:48.560 --> 00:10:49.730
What brings you here all of a sudden?

00:10:49.730 --> 00:10:52.690
Don't tell me you've decided on a wedding date already.

00:10:54.150 --> 00:10:56.470
Wedding dresses take time, you know.

00:10:56.470 --> 00:10:57.940
Let me know as soon as you two decide on a date, okay?

00:10:58.070 --> 00:10:59.190
I will.

00:10:59.650 --> 00:11:02.450
Why don't I take your size since you're here?

00:11:02.700 --> 00:11:04.700
No, let's do that some other time.

00:11:06.790 --> 00:11:08.200
Say, Chelin...

00:11:08.790 --> 00:11:10.750
You're here because of Minhyung, aren't you?

00:11:12.460 --> 00:11:14.000
I knew you'd come.

00:11:14.840 --> 00:11:17.460
I actually regretted introducing him to you guys.

00:11:17.920 --> 00:11:20.400
I thought maybe I had disturbed some old memories or something.

00:11:21.170 --> 00:11:22.970
He really looks like him, doesn't he?

00:11:23.470 --> 00:11:27.100
Where did you meet him?

00:11:27.390 --> 00:11:28.810
Where?

00:11:29.890 --> 00:11:32.360
Tell me, Chelin.

00:11:32.360 --> 00:11:34.860
How did you meet him?

00:11:34.980 --> 00:11:35.930
I really want to know—

00:11:35.930 --> 00:11:38.610
No, I <i>need</i> to know.

00:11:39.280 --> 00:11:41.650
Were you really born in America?

00:11:41.650 --> 00:11:42.820
Where did you grow up?

00:11:43.490 --> 00:11:45.300
So you've never been to Korea, then?

00:11:45.300 --> 00:11:46.490
Not even once?

00:11:49.950 --> 00:11:52.660
Yes, but why do you ask?

00:11:54.040 --> 00:11:57.460
He's in no way related to Joonsang.

00:11:57.630 --> 00:11:59.840
Joonsang's dead, as you know.

00:12:00.460 --> 00:12:02.840
He doesn't know anything about Joonsang either.

00:12:02.970 --> 00:12:04.990
He'd be heartbroken if he found out

00:12:04.990 --> 00:12:08.850
that I fell in love with him because he reminds me of someone.

00:12:09.850 --> 00:12:10.810
Don't you think?

00:12:12.350 --> 00:12:13.770
Oh hi, Minhyung.

00:12:14.310 --> 00:12:15.310
Hi.

00:12:16.860 --> 00:12:19.860
I don't think I can make it to the store today.

00:12:20.940 --> 00:12:22.650
I don't know when I'll be done with all this work.

00:12:24.150 --> 00:12:26.200
Sorry, I'll make it there tomorrow; I promise.

00:12:26.450 --> 00:12:28.660
Why don't we take a break to eat?

00:12:27.560 --> 00:12:28.660
Okay.

00:12:28.950 --> 00:12:32.330
Here's your dinner, Mr. Director.

00:12:30.790 --> 00:12:32.330
All right.

00:12:32.870 --> 00:12:34.210
Thank you, Hyeoksoo.

00:12:34.790 --> 00:12:36.970
So I'm "Deputy Manager" when we're working,

00:12:36.970 --> 00:12:38.670
but you call me by my first name when I'm getting your dinner?

00:12:39.710 --> 00:12:42.300
Don't be like that, Hyeoksoo.

00:12:43.550 --> 00:12:45.150
You smooth talker, you.

00:12:45.300 --> 00:12:48.390
By the way, we rescheduled the presentation date with Polaris.

00:12:49.180 --> 00:12:51.900
Oh yeah, wasn't Miss Yujin Jung here earlier?

00:12:51.900 --> 00:12:53.640
Did you guys not wrap up the contract?

00:12:54.430 --> 00:12:55.690
Yujin Jung...

00:12:56.020 --> 00:12:58.400
Do I have a sad-looking face, Hyeoksoo?

00:12:59.020 --> 00:13:00.520
What?

00:13:10.620 --> 00:13:11.450
Yujin.

00:13:19.040 --> 00:13:20.610
You don't look so good.

00:13:20.610 --> 00:13:22.630
Did the presentation not go very well?

00:13:24.130 --> 00:13:24.880
Yeah.

00:13:25.260 --> 00:13:26.420
So it didn't go well.

00:13:26.720 --> 00:13:29.680
Was it because of that new director?

00:13:30.010 --> 00:13:30.720
Huh?

00:13:31.350 --> 00:13:33.430
Isn't he kind of strange?

00:13:33.430 --> 00:13:34.930
Why's he being like this to you?

00:13:35.350 --> 00:13:37.190
Yeah, he's strange.

00:13:37.440 --> 00:13:39.310
He's really strange.

00:13:40.190 --> 00:13:42.470
It's okay, things don't always work out,

00:13:42.470 --> 00:13:43.610
but I'm here.

00:13:43.780 --> 00:13:45.820
You'll always have me, Yujin.

00:13:46.360 --> 00:13:49.530
So try to let it go, okay?

00:13:50.200 --> 00:13:52.530
About that new director...

00:13:52.660 --> 00:13:55.620
Yeah, don't worry about it so much.

00:13:55.870 --> 00:13:58.020
You already have enough to worry about

00:13:58.020 --> 00:13:59.500
outside of work right now, don't you?

00:14:06.670 --> 00:14:10.220
Oh yeah, Polaris is supposed to come over with the contract today.

00:14:10.340 --> 00:14:12.220
You better get ready; they'll be here soon.

00:14:13.180 --> 00:14:14.970
Why are you messing with that puzzle now?

00:14:17.770 --> 00:14:19.730
Did you find this piece, Hyeoksoo?

00:14:19.850 --> 00:14:22.150
What now?

00:14:23.320 --> 00:14:24.390
That's strange.

00:14:24.390 --> 00:14:26.110
I couldn't find it anywhere.

00:14:26.820 --> 00:14:28.450
That's what you're worried about?

00:14:28.900 --> 00:14:33.580
Do you really have that many women you want to remember?

00:14:33.870 --> 00:14:34.530
Excuse me?

00:14:35.620 --> 00:14:39.080
I didn't get why you keep bothering yourself with puzzles,

00:14:39.660 --> 00:14:41.210
but I think I do now.

00:14:41.790 --> 00:14:43.590
What are you talking about?

00:14:43.960 --> 00:14:49.800
Miss Yujin Jung from Polaris told me something very memorable

00:14:49.920 --> 00:14:52.340
when I said I didn't understand why you bothered yourself with puzzles:

00:14:52.800 --> 00:14:57.350
she said "maybe he has things he wants to remember piece-by-piece."

00:14:57.560 --> 00:15:01.140
I was right about the woman thing, wasn't I?

00:15:03.060 --> 00:15:05.300
One piece of the puzzle represents one woman,

00:15:05.300 --> 00:15:07.480
while two pieces represent two women.

00:15:07.780 --> 00:15:08.490
Good for you.

00:15:08.610 --> 00:15:10.400
The representative from Polaris is here.

00:15:12.660 --> 00:15:14.870
Hello, nice to meet you.

00:15:15.160 --> 00:15:17.120
I didn't expect you to come yourself, Jeong-a.

00:15:20.500 --> 00:15:22.870
Born in New York. Moved to Paris...

00:15:27.710 --> 00:15:29.590
I'm back, Yujin.

00:15:30.670 --> 00:15:31.840
Did you land the contract?

00:15:32.590 --> 00:15:33.720
Tada.

00:15:34.090 --> 00:15:35.940
Let's go eat; it's on me.

00:15:35.940 --> 00:15:37.510
What do you wanna eat, Yujin?

00:15:39.720 --> 00:15:41.680
Say, Jeong-a...

00:15:42.190 --> 00:15:42.980
What?

00:15:43.350 --> 00:15:45.520
...you really did land the contract, right?

00:15:45.650 --> 00:15:47.730
Of course I did.

00:15:48.230 --> 00:15:53.740
MARCIAN did have one condition though.

00:15:54.240 --> 00:15:55.950
What kind of condition?

00:15:56.570 --> 00:16:00.540
That ever-so-handsome Minhyung Lee insisted on it;

00:16:00.910 --> 00:16:05.040
"Yujin Jung is to spearhead this project on behalf of Polaris."

00:16:05.750 --> 00:16:08.550
That's asking too much!

00:16:09.380 --> 00:16:13.050
You need to finish what you began, starting with the presentation.

00:16:14.260 --> 00:16:17.010
Didn't I tell you that I'm not going to do it?

00:16:18.300 --> 00:16:23.520
The focus of this renovation is an eco-friendly design.

00:16:24.350 --> 00:16:25.790
The focus of our renovation project

00:16:25.790 --> 00:16:29.360
is to emphasize the harmony found in the beauty of the surroundings

00:16:29.480 --> 00:16:34.950
coming together with a modern conceptual design.

00:16:36.070 --> 00:16:38.580
If I can get you to agree with the overall outline,

00:16:38.740 --> 00:16:41.930
we should be able to adjust the minor details,

00:16:41.930 --> 00:16:44.330
so long as it's within the boundaries of the conceptual design.

00:16:45.210 --> 00:16:47.790
Do you always work like this, Miss Yujin?

00:16:48.130 --> 00:16:48.540
Excuse me?

00:16:48.540 --> 00:16:50.300
I'm not saying that it's bad,

00:16:51.590 --> 00:16:54.590
but you sounded like a student giving a presentation after an all-nighter.

00:16:54.800 --> 00:16:59.510
Please elaborate on what it is that you'd like me to explain better

00:16:59.680 --> 00:17:01.810
and I'll gladly explain it to you.

00:17:06.020 --> 00:17:08.480
Do I make you uncomfortable, Miss Yujin?

00:17:09.230 --> 00:17:11.980
I like to think that a good partnership is very important for things like this,

00:17:12.610 --> 00:17:14.090
but we're bound to have conflicts down the road

00:17:14.090 --> 00:17:16.280
if we're having problems before we're even partners.

00:17:17.110 --> 00:17:19.450
Whereas I do think that it's important to like the work that you do,

00:17:19.620 --> 00:17:23.290
I don't feel the same way about your clientèle.

00:17:24.450 --> 00:17:26.920
So your work and your clients are two different things?

00:17:29.330 --> 00:17:31.520
I probably would have stopped working a long time ago,

00:17:31.520 --> 00:17:34.130
if I had only worked with people I liked.

00:17:35.670 --> 00:17:37.080
In other words,

00:17:37.080 --> 00:17:38.840
you like the work that you've been given,

00:17:39.840 --> 00:17:42.260
but you don't like me, is that right?

00:17:42.930 --> 00:17:46.390
I apologize if I came off like that.

00:17:46.520 --> 00:17:48.600
I actually have to like the people I work with too.

00:17:49.020 --> 00:17:52.070
I don't think I could object if you were to cancel our contract

00:17:52.070 --> 00:17:53.270
because you're uncomfortable with me.

00:17:55.320 --> 00:17:56.490
But what can I do?

00:17:58.280 --> 00:17:59.730
I want to proceed with this project.

00:17:59.730 --> 00:18:01.160
I like having you on board.

00:18:12.170 --> 00:18:13.000
Hey, Yujin!

00:18:13.630 --> 00:18:15.340
How did you know I was here?

00:18:16.710 --> 00:18:17.550
It's a secret.

00:18:20.890 --> 00:18:23.020
I was talking to Jeong-a on the phone

00:18:23.020 --> 00:18:25.850
and she said you were presenting here, so I came to cheer you on.

00:18:26.180 --> 00:18:27.310
It must have been hard.

00:18:28.100 --> 00:18:29.230
I'm fine.

00:18:29.810 --> 00:18:30.680
How was the presentation?

00:18:30.680 --> 00:18:31.960
Did it turn out okay?

00:18:31.960 --> 00:18:33.820
I heard you guys landed the contract.

00:18:34.610 --> 00:18:35.530
Yeah.

00:18:35.980 --> 00:18:37.320
That's good, then.

00:18:37.570 --> 00:18:39.400
Let's go, you must be hungry.

00:18:39.610 --> 00:18:40.820
Right.

00:18:41.910 --> 00:18:44.200
Wait a second, Miss Yujin.

00:18:44.200 --> 00:18:45.240
Are you leaving?

00:18:45.400 --> 00:18:46.530
Yes.

00:18:46.660 --> 00:18:48.750
Thank you for all the hard work up to this point,

00:18:48.870 --> 00:18:52.210
but this is where it really begins, so let's try our best together.

00:18:52.330 --> 00:18:54.750
Thank you, I'll do my best.

00:18:54.960 --> 00:18:55.880
I'll be seeing you then.

00:18:56.210 --> 00:18:57.380
Take care.

00:18:58.800 --> 00:19:02.310
So that's the horrible director I've been hearing about.

00:19:02.310 --> 00:19:03.090
Right?

00:19:03.220 --> 00:19:04.850
No, that's...

00:19:04.970 --> 00:19:06.830
I can tell he's horrible just from the way he looks.

00:19:06.830 --> 00:19:08.180
Want me to say something to him?

00:19:09.020 --> 00:19:11.310
Stop bullying my Yujin!

00:19:11.440 --> 00:19:12.850
Stop that!

00:19:12.980 --> 00:19:14.060
Fine, fine.

00:19:19.110 --> 00:19:21.240
It's so much hard work, Minhyung.

00:19:21.650 --> 00:19:23.500
I'm so busy running the store

00:19:23.500 --> 00:19:26.200
that I don't even have time to prepare for the fashion show.

00:19:26.580 --> 00:19:28.220
Picking out clothes

00:19:28.220 --> 00:19:30.620
and putting them on a bunch of girls shouldn't be so hard.

00:19:30.790 --> 00:19:34.080
Just think of it like playing with dolls, and you'll do fine.

00:19:34.580 --> 00:19:38.550
At least dolls don't bitch at you about every little thing.

00:19:39.590 --> 00:19:40.300
I guess they don't.

00:19:40.920 --> 00:19:42.310
Oh yeah,

00:19:42.310 --> 00:19:45.340
there's this new interior designer that we're working with.

00:19:46.300 --> 00:19:48.180
Should I tell you who it is?

00:19:48.930 --> 00:19:49.950
Why?

00:19:49.950 --> 00:19:51.270
It's a woman, isn't it?

00:19:51.520 --> 00:19:55.350
She must be one heck of a beauty for you to show some interest.

00:19:55.940 --> 00:19:58.320
You look a little nervous there.

00:19:58.730 --> 00:20:00.280
You wish!

00:20:00.610 --> 00:20:02.650
I wouldn't be surprised if you were.

00:20:03.280 --> 00:20:06.620
She's got talent, and she's not bad looking.

00:20:07.870 --> 00:20:11.080
She's also got this weird charm about her.

00:20:11.660 --> 00:20:13.250
You still don't want to know who it is?

00:20:13.580 --> 00:20:14.670
I'm not interested.

00:20:15.540 --> 00:20:18.250
What I <i>am</i> interested in, however,

00:20:18.790 --> 00:20:22.340
is when are you going to get a grip and settle down, Minhyung?

00:20:23.260 --> 00:20:24.380
What are you talking about?

00:20:24.550 --> 00:20:25.530
I mean come on,

00:20:25.530 --> 00:20:27.640
isn't it weird that you've been in Korea for two months already

00:20:28.300 --> 00:20:32.230
and you're still living in a hotel?

00:20:32.730 --> 00:20:33.980
I told you.

00:20:33.980 --> 00:20:36.190
I'm going to live in a house that I've built myself.

00:20:36.350 --> 00:20:37.280
You're still talking about that?

00:20:37.280 --> 00:20:40.610
I hope that's going to be one impressive house.

00:20:42.320 --> 00:20:47.570
Do you know what the sturdiest and most beautiful house in this world is?

00:20:47.820 --> 00:20:48.530
You tell me.

00:20:48.660 --> 00:20:51.620
It's a house that you build inside the heart of the one you love.

00:20:53.500 --> 00:20:56.080
Then why don't you build one right now?

00:20:58.540 --> 00:21:00.130
Not yet. {oooh rejected.}

00:21:04.010 --> 00:21:05.930
<i>I was supposed to go look at the ski resort with Deputy Manager Kim,</i>

00:21:05.930 --> 00:21:08.300
<i>but I don't think I can go because Happy's really sick.</i>

00:21:08.430 --> 00:21:10.630
<i>I'm at the pet hospital right now; you'll have to take my place.</i>

00:21:10.630 --> 00:21:11.890
<i>I'm hanging up, Yujin; thanks a lot!</i>

00:21:12.010 --> 00:21:12.970
Jeong-a...

00:21:13.640 --> 00:21:14.600
Jeong-a!

00:21:17.520 --> 00:21:18.900
What did you say your pet's name was?

00:21:19.310 --> 00:21:20.730
Happy. It's Happy.

00:21:20.980 --> 00:21:21.940
Happy, you say?

00:21:21.940 --> 00:21:24.030
This dog's not Happy.

00:21:24.570 --> 00:21:26.950
It's Unhappy I tell you, Unhappy.

00:21:27.530 --> 00:21:28.860
It's not happy.

00:21:29.320 --> 00:21:30.490
Your dog is depressed.

00:21:31.620 --> 00:21:34.410
From the looks of it, you seem to live alone.

00:21:34.660 --> 00:21:36.580
You don't go home very often, do you?

00:21:37.710 --> 00:21:38.670
What did you say?

00:21:38.790 --> 00:21:40.880
And of course, you probably don't have a man.

00:21:41.710 --> 00:21:44.980
Forcing solitude on your pet just because you yourself have a hard life

00:21:44.980 --> 00:21:46.880
is violence, I tell you.

00:21:47.220 --> 00:21:48.350
Do you understand what I'm saying?

00:21:48.350 --> 00:21:49.260
It's violence!

00:21:50.220 --> 00:21:51.180
Excuse me?

00:21:51.720 --> 00:21:55.080
So if this fella here was a real kid and not a puppy,

00:21:55.620 --> 00:22:00.270
you would have been arrested already for child abuse.

00:22:01.020 --> 00:22:03.400
So violence is bad, m'kay?

00:22:03.820 --> 00:22:05.940
How rude.

00:22:06.030 --> 00:22:08.440
Give him to me, I'm taking him to a different hospital.

00:22:08.440 --> 00:22:09.360
Give him to me!

00:22:09.490 --> 00:22:10.780
Did you hear what I said?

00:22:12.580 --> 00:22:15.750
You're so daring to link arms with someone who you've only just met.

00:22:16.660 --> 00:22:19.650
All right, since it's come to this,

00:22:19.650 --> 00:22:21.270
I'll treat him with all my heart

00:22:21.400 --> 00:22:25.590
and change him back from Unhappy to Happy.

00:22:26.460 --> 00:22:27.300
Huh?

00:22:27.590 --> 00:22:28.920
Look at you, Happy.

00:22:30.840 --> 00:22:32.930
Don't worry, be happy.

00:22:33.220 --> 00:22:34.890
Oh geez.

00:22:57.660 --> 00:22:58.700
Miss Yujin?

00:23:04.130 --> 00:23:06.420
I thought Deputy Manager Kim was supposed to come?

00:23:07.170 --> 00:23:09.800
I didn't think <i>you</i> would be coming either.

00:23:11.470 --> 00:23:14.010
He had something to take care of, so I figured I'd go instead.

00:23:14.600 --> 00:23:15.390
Hop in.

00:23:18.470 --> 00:23:20.020
It's getting late, come on.

00:23:35.990 --> 00:23:36.870
Hey, Yujin. {this line is supposed to be dramatic because he calls her without formalities, kinda like how Joonsang used to.}
